Remove the public principal from the bucket policy. Replace
`"Principal": "*"` with specific IAM ARNs, or delete the policy statement entirely if public access was unintentional. Then enable all four
public-access-block settings:
resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "this" {
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

Replace the wildcard policy with least-privilege statements. List only the
actions the workload needs on only the ARNs it touches:
policy = jsonencode({
  Version = "2012-10-17"
  Statement = [{
    Effect   = "Allow"
    Action   = ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"]
    Resource = ["arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*"]
  }]
})
Use IAM Access Analyzer policy generation from CloudTrail to derive the minimum set.

